## Circuit Breaker State Machine

The enterprise Circuit Breaker operates as a state machine with three strictly defined states: **Closed**, **Open**, and **Half-Open**:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph States["Circuit Breaker State Machine"]
        Closed["1. Closed (Normal Operation)\n• All HTTP requests pass to network\n• Successes reset failure count\n• 3 consecutive 5xx/timeouts trip breaker"]
        Open["2. Open (Fault Tripped)\n• Requests fail-fast immediately\n• Zero network calls executed\n• Serves local encrypted cache\n• Starts 30s reset timer"]
        HalfOpen["3. Half-Open (Canary Probe)\n• Reset timer expires\n• Allows single trial request\n• If success: resets to Closed\n• If failure: returns to Open"]

        Closed -->|"Failure threshold exceeded (3 errors)"| Open
        Open -->|"Reset timeout expires (30s)"| HalfOpen
        HalfOpen -->|"Canary probe succeeds"| Closed
        HalfOpen -->|"Canary probe fails"| Open
    end

