## Standard Configuration Parameters

Enterprise mobile applications must initialize circuit breakers using these standardized operational parameters:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Configuration Parameter</th>
        <th>Recommended Value</th>
        <th>Behavioral Impact</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>failureThreshold</code></td>
        <td><code>3 consecutive failures</code></td>
        <td>Number of 5xx server errors or socket timeouts before transitioning from <strong>Closed</strong> to <strong>Open</strong>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>requestTimeoutMs</code></td>
        <td><code>5,000 ms (5 seconds)</code></td>
        <td>Maximum duration for an individual network request before considering it a timeout failure.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>resetTimeoutMs</code></td>
        <td><code>30,000 ms (30 seconds)</code></td>
        <td>Duration the breaker remains in <strong>Open</strong> before allowing a canary probe in <strong>Half-Open</strong>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>maxRetriesWithBackoff</code></td>
        <td><code>2 retries</code></td>
        <td>Exponential backoff with jitter applied only while in <strong>Closed</strong> state before counting as a failure.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ignoredErrorCodes</code></td>
        <td><code>400, 401, 403, 404, 422</code></td>
        <td>Client-side 4xx errors <strong>never</strong> trip the breaker because they represent validation or auth issues, not backend outages.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

