## Architectural Anti-Patterns & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">RESILIENCE ANTI-PATTERNS</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. Tripping on 4xx Errors:</strong> Never increment the failure count for HTTP 400, 401, 403, or 404 responses. These represent client validation or credential issues, not server degradation.</li>
    <li><strong>2. Infinite While-Loop Retries:</strong> Never implement unconstrained `while (!success)` retry loops on mobile clients. All retries must be capped at 2 iterations with exponential backoff plus jitter.</li>
    <li><strong>3. Uncached Fallbacks:</strong> Do not use a Circuit Breaker without an offline local storage fallback. Failing fast with an empty screen offers no UX benefit over a regular error.</li>
    <li><strong>4. Global Monolithic Breakers:</strong> Never use a single global circuit breaker instance for all app APIs. Each domain microservice (e.g., Orders, Identity, Catalog) must have its own independent circuit instance.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

